{"trans": "Advocate for fair competition, oppose deception and trickery, and promote a flourishing diversity of content online; advocate for unity and cooperation, oppose harming others for self-interest, and promote mutual benefit and win-win situations on the internet."}
{"trans": "All in all, perhaps more overseas companies consider that listing in the United States is not worth the cost, so they choose to withdraw as the best strategy, but this by no means implies that they are ready to abandon the US market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a panic-stricken market environment, it is extremely difficult for gold to remain unaffected. To talk rashly about breaking the $1000 mark is probably just another pipe dream."}
{"trans": "The police officer explained that the actions of these students were an act of bravery, as they stepped forward at the critical moment when the elderly person fell into the water, which is very commendable. According to reports, the elderly person has minor mental health issues and, after full rescue efforts at the hospital, has been out of danger."}
{"trans": "Of course, the methods mentioned above are just a few of the limited yet effective approaches for review. The arrangements for the final review sprint should be varied and diverse, and choices should be made based on the individual characteristics of each candidate. Wishing all candidates a triumphant start and immediate success!"}
{"trans": "Flowing into another long river in this lifetime\nThe place where Zhaojun dismounted\nThe stones riding history are still speaking\nThe grass is as green as in those years\nThe flowers carry the fragrance of the past\nA flock of cattle and sheep don't recognize today\nBowing their heads, modest and cautious\nIn the meticulous time\nDrinking water and remembering its source\nPeople sit in the fragrance of wine\nAutumn waters of South Lake, smokeless night"}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking a life of idle contentment, nor about living to be a hundred years old. Since one cannot live twice, how can one realize the meaning and value of life before death. Even if reduced to dust, one must leave a clear, resonant sound like jade striking the ground, and let the light of life shine forth in the world."}
{"trans": "While the others were able to remain calm, holding their guns and observing the enemy situation all around, only Li Wenbin was in a panic, diving headfirst into the grass with his rear end high in the air, covering his head with his hands in utter disarray. His companions covered their faces and snickered, and Li Wenbin's prestige immediately plummeted."}
{"trans": "\"How do you plan to be king?\" the animals asked half-doubtingly. \"First, mediate disputes impartially, fairly, and reasonably. Second, handle state affairs diligently and without complaint. Third, when facing powerful enemies, lead from the front and charge ahead. This is my inaugural speech.\""}
{"trans": "He was worldly-wise, having experienced the vicissitudes of life, and could change direction like a compass needle. His North Star was fickle and not fixed. Thanks to his pleasing sweet talk, he was so despicable that he never came to harm; furthermore, he was eloquent and talked endlessly (unless not paid enough)."}
{"trans": "The first time I followed my colleague to the securities exchange, I was destined to form an indissoluble bond with stocks. Over seventeen spring and autumn seasons, I have fully tasted the ups and downs of the stock market. After several ups and downs, I have become a veteran, and past events are still vivid in my memory! 1. The sea of bitterness is boundless, turn back to the shore."}
{"trans": "The defeated soldiers fled for a long time before stopping. He looked up to the sky and sighed: \"I started my army at twenty-five, invincible in battle, unstoppable in attack. Now, in my twilight years, I have suffered such a disastrous defeat. It truly infuriates me!\" The news of the victory in the Battle of Ningyuan reached the imperial court, and everyone from top to bottom was ecstatic. They all raised their glasses to celebrate."}
{"trans": "Newlyweds receive an endless stream of relatives and friends coming to offer their blessings. Since the living room arrangement shouldn't be too unconventional, it should focus on comfort and warmth. It needs to be comfortable for the couple to live in while also making guests feel at home. Soft fabric sofas and pillows are essential elements."}
{"trans": "I said, stop making wild analogies, let's just stick to the matter at hand. My son said, after observing your attitude coldly for many years, I feel you treat the computer as something sacred. You don't dare to touch this, and you can't touch that. The biggest psychological barrier for you mothers when learning is that you treat the computer like a deity."}
{"trans": "Always being anxious, afraid of saying the wrong thing, afraid of doing the wrong thing, afraid of offending people. The seventh precept is sorrow: Throughout one's life, some unfortunate events often appear before one's eyes, and one can't help but feel sorrow arising from within. The eighth precept is suspicion: Those with a suspicious mind always think that others are scheming against them, and they have to be on guard with every word and action, thus becoming restless and often suffering from insomnia."}
{"trans": "In the previous shameful corner, there was also a pitiful guillotine, sneaky, panicky, and disgraceful, as if always in constant fear, lest it be caught on the spot doing bad things—because it would immediately make a quick getaway after finishing its dirty work each time. How could one not feel gratified by all of this!"}
{"trans": "At this time, the real charm of fighting lies in the anticipation after arranging a fight, the tension before the fight, the verbal sparring when mediating, the drinking and celebration after the fight ends, the righteousness when meeting again in the future, and fighting side by side in the next fight. This cycle repeats, and the ranks of pacifism grow stronger and larger."}
{"trans": "The Baron's such brazen insults are simply unbearable; Just wait, you shameless madman, for honor, I will take on the responsibility of revenge. Faced with such brazen insults from everyone, only he can bear the responsibility of revenge; Even if it costs him his life, he cannot endure this humiliation in silence."}
{"trans": "It seemed there would be no argument, no storm, and all was calm now. But Mother once again asked an untimely question: \"Do you want to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" The daughter's answer was also strange and untimely: \"Later, good mother, let's look later.\""}
{"trans": "When it comes to conducting himself in society, he is still at a beginner's stage, but when it comes to knowledge, he is confident and well-prepared. No matter how eloquent a department director may be, he might not be more tricky and eccentric than the professors on a master's thesis defense committee. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat Western food, he might be at a loss, but if you ask him how to chop firewood, isn't that something he can do with ease?!"}
{"trans": "\"You will soon reap the consequences of your idleness.\" After saying this, the ox lowered its head under the yoke and pulled its cart full of manure away. \"You should live an honest and upright life, and be careful throughout your life not to be lazy and idle. If you still feel no shame, you will surely suffer the consequences of your own actions.\""}
{"trans": "He painted it, and painted it so vividly and lifelike. His art repeatedly deceived people's eyes, making them at first glance mistake it for a real object, not realizing it was a painting. For hundreds of years, this painting art, which had always been considered vulgar and not refined, was only in his hands once again glorified and developed."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been mythologized by people to the point of being sacred and inviolable, mysterious and unfathomable, thus worshipped as if they were heavenly gods, hence the title \"Son of Heaven\". In reality, emperors are also human, with both good and bad qualities. Among emperors, there have been enlightened rulers with great talent and vision who bring peace and stability to the nation, as well as incompetent and foolish tyrants."}
{"trans": "Once upon a time, he \"laughed loudly to the sky as he went out the door,\" loudly reciting \"how could people like us be ordinary folk?\" The deception and scheming in official circles, the pretentious righteousness in secular society, the ruthless reality cooled his once-passionate spirit. How could the golden canopy of a \"court scholar\" possibly cover your unrestrained and free-spirited heart? Finally, after experiencing setbacks and pain in your official career, you found peace."}
{"trans": "\"A suspicious vagrant has been harassing our territory for some time, stirring up trouble and sowing discord. You are ordered to capture this troublemaker and execute him by tomorrow.\"\"We'll certainly follow your orders, sir.\" The police officers said and then left. The villain, being one-eyed, didn't notice them winking at each other as they replied."}
{"trans": "Americans have never treated their national leaders as deities, nor would they obey them unconditionally. However, Obama succumbed to the expectations of his supporters. He also believed himself to be the long-awaited savior they expected. The silence of the people dealt him a heavy blow. But the feeling of rising to heaven in a single bound was so intoxicating that it almost made him forget himself."}
{"trans": "A Taurus man who is usually cheerful, with a thoroughly pragmatic personality, cannot tolerate betrayal. Don't attempt to probe his true feelings; the steady bull is content with grazing and eating grass, and smiles at you like Jesus looking at his sheep. If you don't want to shift the scene to a Spanish bullfighting arena to witness the horrific sight of blood flowing like rivers and bodies lying everywhere, never make him jealous."}
{"trans": "Without playing little tricks and using clever schemes, where would Gemini find joy in life? Don't be fooled by his usual nonchalant attitude; once the situation becomes complicated, he will catch you completely by surprise. While everyone else is fighting fiercely, he can sit back and reap the benefits. Yet once he successfully captures everyone's attention, he'll casually walk away like a carefree prince, playing the game of feigned retreat with you."}
{"trans": "In reality, being in the eurozone and bound by the euro, it is simply a fantasy for Germans to remain unscathed. When the eurozone was initially established, it embraced the grand vision of shared prosperity. Now that the Greek debt crisis has triggered the European debt crisis, it is only natural that they suffer together. When the city gate catches fire, the fish in the moat suffer, especially when the surroundings are already filled with flames of war, and some places have almost become scorched earth."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, directly investing in commodities may be the most direct and effective way to hedge against inflation. However, when it comes to commodity investment, what often comes to mind first are some shocking stories, such as those who went bankrupt trading commodity futures, or airlines that suffered huge losses from crude oil hedging, to name just a few. It seems that the risks of commodity investment are so high that ordinary people are deterred from getting involved."}
{"trans": "The vast sky endures the ravages of lightning and thunder, and that's why there are gentle winds and beautiful sunshine; the vast ocean tolerates the rampage of terrifying waves, and that's why there are clear, rippling waves; the silent forest endures the cruelty of the law of the jungle, and that's why there is the beauty of birds singing and flowers fragrant. The sky, ocean, and forest, precisely because they understand tolerance, know when to yield, and bow down to accept, have achieved beauty and extraordinariness. When one humbles oneself, the world becomes broad."}
{"trans": "Surveying the changing landscape of the college entrance examination in recent years, what we need is to firmly grasp the new trends and directions of exam questions, plan ahead, and move from seeing flowers in the fog to having a crystal-clear perspective. Only then can you be as prepared as an army of a million elite soldiers, ready to battle on the examination field and effortlessly defeat your challenges. With expert guidance that turns iron into gold; remembering that a journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step and a nine-story platform rises from a pile of earth—we help you successfully take the first step in your college entrance exam review!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate yourself is like having the golden key to obtaining happiness. Appreciating yourself is not narcissism, appreciating yourself is not arrogance, appreciating yourself is not self-indulgence, and appreciating yourself is certainly not being closed-minded... Give yourself some confidence, give yourself a little joy, give yourself a smile, why worry about not having happiness in life? Often create celebrations for yourself, learn to find joyful moods."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people are gradually realizing that the internet and traditional industries are not mortal enemies in a life-or-death struggle, but can be a \"perfect match\" that complement each other beautifully. The retail industry is gradually showing characteristics of channel integration, with mutual penetration and integration between online and offline gradually increasing. Currently, Taobao has already opened offline stores, while traditional enterprises entering the internet space are as numerous as carp crossing the river. From Gome and Suning to Walmart and Carrefour supermarkets, the list goes on and on."}
{"trans": "In summary, uncertainties in the commodity market continue to emerge, and financial hegemony still manipulates the market with frequently changing rules. Against the backdrop of the global debt crisis and mixed prospects for world economic recovery, the US dollar remains the most important factor affecting the trend of bulk commodities. European and American economic policies follow closely, while domestic regulations exacerbate the situation. The interplay of funding and confidence aspects from these three intertwined factors will inevitably cause severe fluctuations in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "China Red is a thought-provoking spiritual culture, unique to the Chinese people. It is a powerful force, embodying self-improvement, sincerity, diligence, kindness, and indomitable spirit. It is a Chinese quality that has been passed down for thousands of years with magnificent vigor. Liantianhong, a leading furniture enterprise, passionately spreads the flame of China Red. With a business philosophy based on integrity, it has pioneered transparent workshop production, setting an industry example and giving the furniture industry a completely new look."}
{"trans": "Characteristics: In \"Journey to the West\", Tang Sanzang is tall in stature, elegant in manner, kind in temperament, and has profound Buddhist knowledge. On his journey to the West to retrieve the Buddhist scriptures, he encountered eighty-one tribulations but remained unwavering in his determination. With the assistance of Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Wujing, he endured countless hardships and finally succeeded in bringing back the true scriptures. Sun Wukong, also known as the Pilgrim, is Tang Sanzang's eldest disciple. He has fiery golden eyes and is capable of seventy-two transformations and cloud-somersaulting. He detests evil as his enemy, fears no difficulties, is persevering, and is brave and fearless."}
{"trans": "3. Regarding studying: I have my own set of experiences—\"developing question intuition\" and \"staying up late less\". Actually, after practice makes perfect in learning, although it may not be effortless, one can have a good grasp of it. I don't advocate the tactic of drowning in practice questions, because there's no need to repeatedly do the same or similar questions. We only need to compare similar questions, reflect deeply, and summarize the methods to solve this type of problem. The so-called \"question intuition\" is similar to what we often call \"language intuition\" in English."}
{"trans": "The world's longest man-made structure - China's Great Wall. The magnificent and spectacular Great Wall of China crosses the peaks of the high mountains and ridges in northern China, with a total length of over 6,700 kilometers. It was first built during the Spring and Autumn Period and the Warring States Period. It is a rare ancient military defense project in the history of human architecture. It is world-renowned for its long history, enormous scale, and magnificent presence. It was listed by UNESCO as a \"World Heritage Site\" and is acclaimed as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\""}
{"trans": "They maintain a low profile because they have the capital to do so; they remain understated because they are extraordinary and cannot conform to the commonplace. Essentially, luxury goods are exceptional, even unique. They permit no compromise in quality or in their representation of fashion, and they possess impeccable superiority in art, culture, and style. While luxury goods are certainly not life's necessities, their unparalleled craftsmanship and rich brand heritage can absolutely make them essential to one's life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as heavy as lead, she still strode across the street toward the parking garage. Now, drowsy and driving alone on the fluorescent cement lane, she felt her consciousness blurring. When she had parked her car here seventeen hours earlier, there had been two minivans parked on either side, so close that she had to squeeze out of her car. Now her old 'Taurus' stood like an orphan, all alone in the eighth level of the parking area."}
{"trans": "Ten years ago, perhaps no one knew that the internet could become mobile with laptops, just as twenty years ago people could not imagine that telephones could be put in pockets, accompanying modern people's work and life at all times. Today, various smart devices are exuding unprecedented magic, subtly changing the way humans live. In the next ten years, in fields such as terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics, more disruptive innovations are very likely to be brewing!"}
{"trans": "We advocate team spirit, and we also admire the heroism of selflessly rescuing comrades, but we must ensure that we don't become a burden to our comrades, and do our best not to let them take unnecessary risks to save us. Strict training and decisive judgment of the situation on the ground are absolutely essential! Before you've experienced real combat, don't play your armchair theorist games in front of us. There are things that a fresh-out-of-school officer like you simply cannot understand!"}
{"trans": "Blame me for not deeply comprehending the five-character poem about the poplar tree and my grandfather's seven-character poem. Although I've made gradual progress in the art of 'playing dumb' through daily accumulation, I haven't achieved complete enlightenment. Last night, my neck was bitten by a silent mosquito, and I shouted loudly: 'How can you bite someone without making a sound? How can you not suck blood openly and honestly? How can you not learn to be an upright mosquito, advancing toward my neck with a roar?' Therefore, I live a tired and absurd life, often hearing the humming laughter of mosquitoes."}
{"trans": "When barbecue restaurants spring up like mushrooms in every corner of the city, people's nights become more flavorful. However, it's truly difficult to enjoy delicious food while also experiencing an elegant environment. As the sun sets and the reddened sky meets the lush green grass of the sports field, in such a beautiful setting, tables are arranged in an orderly fashion according to the terrain. The barbecue chefs skillfully grill the food, waiters shuttle about, and customers chat and laugh, all enjoying themselves. Soothing music plays in the ears, creating a charming atmosphere."}
{"trans": "When I said this, the old gentleman sighed deeply: \"Oh, I've survived so many near-death experiences, it's really hard to put into words!\" And so, this old gentleman who was naturally proud and stubborn finally opened up about his rough life and inner world to me, a writer he had never met before, for the first time... In his narration, which was at times passionate, at times heavy, at times filled with tears, and at times with hearty laughter, I could feel the magnificent yet tragic life of this seventy-year-old man who had experienced many hardships, and the uncontrollable arrangements of fate..."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, the Western political scene is far from clean as people imagine. Beneath the appearance of integrity, there is a surge of sludge and dirty water, though this sludge has a uniquely Western flavor. On stage, they \"sow seeds\" with grandeur, while off stage, they \"reap\" legally and reasonably. Between calculating politicians and shrewd capitalists, there is a tacit understanding and默契 cooperation. The game of exchanging favors and power-for-money transactions between officials and businessmen is played with such skill that it becomes open and legal, so skillful that Western democracy and rule of law are powerless against it."}
{"trans": "After wading through water for several hours, a vast, open cavern suddenly came into view. \"Good heavens, this isn't an underground cave at all, but a veritable underground forest,\" the team member exclaimed. The cavern was as large as a basketball court, with rugged rocks, gurgling streams, and crisscrossing ravines on the ground. Stalagmites as thick as bowls grew over ten meters high, accompanied by massive stone curtains, jagged stone hangings, and intertwined stone pillars... It was a bizarre landscape resembling a primeval forest. Moreover, numerous crystals sparkled under the light, making one feel as if they had entered a fairy tale world while walking through it."}
{"trans": "The scale of the heart can also shrink very, very small, able to hold only a home, a person, a sesame seed, or a drop of virus. A thread of rain can drown it. A wisp of wind can shatter it. A rumor can make it suffer unbearably. A conspiracy can doom it to eternal damnation. The heart can be very hard, harder than any known metal in the world. The heart can be very soft, like a lament, like silk, like satin. The heart can be very resilient; after thousands of times of being bent and wronged, it remains as smooth as ever. The heart can be very brittle; with one careless moment, it can suddenly shatter like fine jade."}
{"trans": "Walking through it, one sees trees providing shade, blooming flowers competing in beauty, serene and quiet scenery that is overwhelming; gentle breeze, fragrant scent assailing the senses, immediately feeling refreshed and relaxed. Winding stone-paved paths lead to secluded spots, with well-arranged flowers and trees, the crisp and pleasant sound of flowing water, multiple scenic elements interweaving three-dimensionally, forming a vibrant and fragrant living picture scroll. Scenes change with each step, every flower, every leaf, every blade of grass, every tree, every stone, every spring, all revealing unique charm, making people distance themselves from the worldly hustle, experiencing the beauty of harmony between nature and humanity, and the cleansing of the soul. Wandering in this beautiful scenery, fully enjoying the earthly pleasures."}
{"trans": "The flustered original whaling ship said: \"This is the whale we caught.\"\nThe triumphant current whaling ship said: \"Then how did it end up with us?\"\nThe flustered party said: \"It escaped again.\"\nThe triumphant party said: \"Who told you not to tie it up properly?\"\nThe flustered party said:"}
{"trans": "Your sanctimonious appearance cannot hide your arrogance and your greed! Pretentious doctors, babbling witches, smooth-tongued swindlers are mocking our incompetence—beware of the slap! You, ungrateful husbands, who think yourselves smart and capable. You despise love and kindness;"}
{"trans": "The two-month farce has come to an end, and it's unclear why Foxconn was so angry about these two reports. Wealthy and powerful companies are not short of think tanks, and crisis PR tactics can include high-profile anger as well as tearful appeals: perhaps to make an example of someone, or perhaps as a diversionary tactic."}
{"trans": "Reward based on merit. Delicious food should rightfully belong to it. \"I see you as pathetic and ridiculous, so arrogant,\" the wild duck replied, \"Your view is flawed. We wild ducks fly to the ends of the earth, free and unattached, making the four seas our home. But you live under others' roof; we support ourselves, while you beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "The beginning of an article is the most difficult part. It needs to be abrupt and vigorous, get straight to the point, and hit the nail on the head in order to captivate the reader. There's no need to beat around the bush or use clichés. He also told me that when reasoning reaches a point of deadlock, a metaphor can resolve all the tangled and difficult arguments effortlessly. How economical! What a skill! All such kinds of wisdom..."}
{"trans": "She began to divine with a straight face. After a flurry of activity, she pretentiously examined the sand tray, made some calculations, then raised her head, stared at Kudi, and said: \"You damned shameless person! How dare you make things up in front of me! The divination makes it perfectly clear: your name is Kudi, and you are a murderous, thieving, unforgivably wicked bandit who stops at no evil.\""}
{"trans": "The castle was indeed like a paradise. He witnessed the magnificent architecture and couldn't help but be captivated, feeling both amazed and envious. They strolled through the garden, picking and eating fresh fruits, immersed in the atmosphere of birdsong and fragrant flowers, so reluctant to leave. When they finished leisurely touring the entire castle, it had already become dark. They returned to the hall beside the pool, planning to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning was indeed quite effective. The cool and fresh air, the well-organized layout, the well-dressed guests, and the courteous waiters—all of this made one feel that this place was a hidden paradise, exceptionally comfortable. It's always people who spoil the scenery. Every one of those well-dressed gentlemen ate until their faces were shiny with grease, which was quite uncomfortable to watch. They all nodded in greeting to Nikolai, and for some reason, some even winked at him."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver. Seeing that their situation was hopeless and the tide had turned against them, they finally gave up resistance and fled toward the city. The armored trains continued to move back and forth, mopping up the remaining enemy forces. They were like two majestic and triumphant land dragons, advancing irresistibly and sweeping away everything in their path. They flattened the enemy's fortress bunkers and sent the slower enemies to their doom. They were a stirring victory declaration by the Chinese army, announcing the coming doom of the stubborn invaders."}
{"trans": "After this calamity, our family never recovered, our fortune declined, and we became impoverished and destitute, struggling in hunger and cold. The old scholar tree lost its former glory as well. The remaining half of the tree stump stood all alone in the half-barren courtyard, exposed to wind and rain, enduring cold dew and frost. For many years, it stood there listlessly, neither sprouting nor growing branches, and no one paid it any attention. It could only stand there stiffly, \"sighing to the heavens.\""}
{"trans": "All reactionary things will not fall if you don't strike them. Dust will not run away on its own without a broom. You are all finished, only I, Zhang Pujing, a loyal Bolshevik, am of noble character and above corruption, half-hearted, flat on my back, prostrate, perfectly smooth, experienced the Marco Polo Bridge Incident, crossing the sea like the Eight Immortals, covering all corners of the land, and absolutely perfect. Haha, revolution is not inviting guests for dinner, not writing an essay, not painting or embroidering, and not frying dough sticks. The proletariat has exercised dictatorship over you monsters and demons."}
{"trans": "Excessive admiration for top scorers in the college entrance examination can make them feel superior to others. Some may develop a complacent mentality, becoming arrogant and self-important, unconsciously relaxing their standards in their future work and life, becoming conservative and finding it difficult to cooperate with others; others may believe they can never be worse than anyone else at any time, excessively pursuing perfection, being overly cautious in their actions, looking forward and backward, and following rules rigidly. All of these factors may cause former top scorers to lack creativity and passion in their endeavors, ultimately making it difficult for them to achieve great things."}
{"trans": "I will treat each of my patients equally, whether their clothes are luxurious or tattered, whether their appearance is handsome or ugly, whether they have abundant money or are in financial difficulty, whether their status is noble or lowly, whether they are immaculate or filled with wounds, whether they have difficult and complicated illnesses or minor ailments, whether they are polite to me or speak rudely, whether they are well-cultured or illiterate, whether they are humorous and witty or dull and boring, whether they are high officials or common people..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That involuntary admiration, that uncontrollable longing, that deep affection of sticking together through thick and thin, that devoted love of supporting each other through difficulties, are precisely life's deepest comfort and most solid support. And all of this is free. Even more, it cannot be bought with money.\n\nGoals are free. Whether it's a prince dressed in fine clothes and eating delicacies, or a ragged homeless child, as long as one is willing, one can set a goal for their life. This goal can be great or ordinary, it can be brilliant or simple, as long as you are willing, you can have it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should concentrate your energy, plan the path to success, and then move forward with all your might. During this time, you cannot be half-hearted, distracted, or change your mind easily. In this process, you should strictly eliminate doubt and fear, because they will undermine your fighting spirit, destroy your motivation to move forward, and affect your actions to achieve your goals with all your might; those who are full of doubt and fear will eventually accomplish nothing and have nothing. When the emotions of doubt and fear sneak into your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all strong thoughts will be severely impacted and collapse."}
{"trans": "A well-educated person is full of respect, awe, and admiration for the various excellent qualities of human beings, such as loyalty, courage, trust, diligence, mutual assistance, self-sacrifice to save others, fearlessness in the face of danger, the ability to endure hardship, and unwavering perseverance. Not everyone can practice these qualities themselves, but they know how to cherish and praise them. It's not that a person cannot be cowardly or lazy, but they cannot disguise these vices as noble virtues, nor can they slander those who have achieved these noble qualities as hypocrites simply because they cannot do so themselves. You may kneel in the mud, but you cannot smear that mud on the chest of the entire world and then solemnly declare that everywhere is filthy."}
{"trans": "In this world, there are silent beginnings, spectacular beginnings, cautious beginnings, bold beginnings, hidden beginnings, reluctant beginnings, beginnings with ulterior motives, and open and upright beginnings. For every journey in life and every matter in daily living, different people will give themselves different ways of beginning. These ways reflect a person's temperament, perspective, courage, magnanimity, and breadth of mind in managing their life."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the review in the final stage serves as the finishing touch for the entire preparation process. Therefore, we should attach great importance to the review in the final stage and at the same time avoid making mistakes that would lead to all previous efforts being wasted and missing success by a narrow margin. Below, I will explain several common pitfalls."}
{"trans": "Currently, the broader market lacks leadership, with large sectors taking turns to adjust. Market support efforts are ineffective, and it's very difficult for mainstream funds to operate. Therefore, the broader market is very weak and jumpy like a startled bird. As soon as there's some negative news, it becomes frightened, leading to intensified panic selling. Off-market funds continue to wait and see, and with the upcoming holiday, the desire to buy is not strong, causing market sentiment to become even more disjointed."}
{"trans": "The stubbornly resisting Japanese were already on their last legs. Their barely holding front line was like a warship full of holes leaking water from all sides. After this fatal blow, it immediately fell apart like weathered rock. In fact, stopping the armored train from advancing was not difficult; one just needed to destroy the railroad tracks in advance."}
{"trans": "Counterfeits: How to Tell Real from Fake? Walnut collectibles are gaining popularity among more and more people, driving market prices up, and counterfeits made with high-tech methods are everywhere. Old Hu was also fooled at first, but now he's experienced and knowledgeable. He even sleeps holding walnuts at night, and basically nothing can deceive him anymore. He shared several methods for distinguishing genuine from fake with the readers of the evening newspaper."}
{"trans": "In my life, much like others, I have walked and crossed both broad, sunny avenues and narrow, single-plank bridges. I've come all this way through a bumpy, winding path. I must admit that I've been fortunate; the success I've achieved and the reputation I've gained are somewhat undeserved. On the other hand, my misfortunes have also been beyond what ordinary people experience. During the so-called 'Great Cultural Revolution,' which was horrifying to hear about, I nearly lost my life for daring to speak out for justice. The physical suffering I endured is also unforgettable for a lifetime."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang can be regarded as one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. He compared himself to Guan Zhong while in Longzhong, what self-confidence this shows! How accurate was his prediction that the empire would be divided into three parts! When he first emerged from his humble dwelling, he faced Xiahou Dun's army of one hundred thousand soldiers without fear; he burned Bowang Slope, making Guan Yu and Zhang Fei completely convinced of his abilities; he burned Xinye, making Cao Ren tremble with fear; his clever strategies in silk pouches, which enraged Zhou Yu three times, showed not only his intelligence but also his sense of humor; he was loyal and devoted, and even though Liu Bei granted him special permission, he did not declare himself emperor; when forced to implement the empty fort strategy due to a tactical error, his calmness was admirable. However, what moves me most is not these achievements, but \"the autumn wind at Wuzhang Plains.\""}
{"trans": "As night falls in the mountain village, we hear waves of sharp, continuous dog barks. After midnight, the barking becomes faint and indistinct, lights in the windows begin to turn on one after another, revealing clean, white faces like the hearts of Chinese cabbages... The moonlight is also washing its face by the water pipe in the courtyard..."}
{"trans": "Shots from close range were blasted over the bar; headers in front of the goal somehow went wide; and even one-on-one opportunities were wasted... Lacking regular playing time in the domestic league, the national youth team's ability to capitalize on scoring chances is lamentable, which is currently the team's biggest weakness."}
{"trans": "But in a sociological sense, today's Palestinian-Israeli parties are mortal enemies. The reason lies both in the fact that after the great exodus of the Jewish people from Palestine in 556 BC, they scattered across the world, causing the two brothers to be separated for more than 1000 years, which led to strangeness, indifference, suspicion, and hostility; and also in the fact that two thousand years later, the Jewish people returned to Palestine to establish the state of Israel. Thus, their mutual struggles turned into massacres, and the brotherly affection completely disappeared."}
{"trans": "National policies descend from above, the industry situation takes a sharp turn for the worse, and ceramic production areas are the first to bear the brunt, like beasts trapped in a predicament. The production areas are struggling, and the ceramic companies are seeking a way out. The cold snap arrives, and while it brings shock and pain to the production areas, it also allows them to see the path to the future more clearly. Detailed reading: The industry situation sharply declines, and many ceramic production areas struggle like trapped beasts."}
{"trans": "Stepping into Suzhou gardens and walking through the courtyards, one might see small bridges over flowing water, white walls and black tiles, or winding paths leading to secluded spots with peaks and turns, or scenes changing with every step, offering infinite variations. The most profound feeling is that their meticulous and refined gardening techniques share the same merits as the imperial gardens of the Forbidden City. The arrangement of corridors, pavilions, and waterside pavilions is layered, progressive, and well-arranged in a staggered pattern. This creates the effect that walking along a 20-meter path gives the visual sensation of 1.5-2.5 kilometers of open space, suddenly making one feel as if they are wandering in a painting."}
{"trans": "The battlefield situation is ever-changing, and there have never been fixed rules for winning battles since ancient times. How to deploy troops and arrange formations, whether to attack or defend, whether to engage in positional warfare or mobile warfare, whether to voluntarily abandon or hold onto a city, which parts to give up and which parts to hold firm—all these should be decided by the frontline commanders themselves, without excessive interference from the supreme commander. In fact, any strategy or tactic can be mastered and applied flexibly; it's hard to say which method is necessarily superior. This is the case of \"all roads lead to Rome\"—winning the battle is the only hard truth."}
{"trans": "A novel is the backlight of the soul. You inject a part of your soul into the work, giving it your flesh and blood, and thus it achieves artistic heights. This involves two issues: first, a writer needs to examine their true state of soul, to first shape yourself; second, the power of sincerity is immense, and its significance here is not only about overcorrection but also about abandoning creative trends that are artificial, sycophantic, sensationalistic, or opportunistic. Don't scratch the surface without reaching the core, don't take off your pants to fart, and don't sell sincerity like a quack remedy. I believe sincerity should be an attitude toward existence, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The weather-beaten locust tree in front of the window,\nThe moon returned to its place, motionless\nHanging on the motionless locust branches\nLike a bell yet so far from the bell's sound\nI know, as for fragments, don't expect them to make a golden sound when they fall to the ground\nYet it is these fragment-like moonbeams\nThat make the silent midnight more like midnight\nA sunken ship"}
{"trans": "Cruel and merciless, cold and heartless, treacherous and sinister, yet I am kind-hearted and softhearted, charitable and generous, saving all living creatures. In the gloomy Dis mansion, my soul attentively drew talismans and characters when suddenly the painful voice of Dulcinea of Toboso came, and only then did I learn that she had unfortunately been enchanted."}
{"trans": "Internet analyst Xu Dandan believes that Alibaba is suspected of burning bridges after crossing them. \"Capital has its own nature, and it's perfectly natural for them to consider their shareholders' interests. Taking over an investment means taking on the capital contract. You can't treat someone like a god when you need them and criticize them like a demon when they become an obstacle.\""}
{"trans": "Even the most perceptive gaze is helpless! The sight is dazzling, not daring to look directly at the throne. We come from the East, but the trouble is in the West; the ranks are vast and long—unable to see the end from the beginning. Those in front fall, and those behind follow, competing eagerly, courage overflowing, with spears in hand, one fights against ten, ten against a hundred, millions of lives vanish without a trace."}
{"trans": "After snatching Zhubailü, just when he was getting carried away with his success, he had to go on a long journey for some reason. When he returned home, he learned from his family members that Zhubailü along with a bag of gold and silver from his house had disappeared without a trace. Upon hearing this news, he flew into a rage, bristling with anger and glaring, he beat and cursed himself, and even tore his clothes. The more he thought about how all his efforts had come to nothing, the angrier he became."}
{"trans": "2008 was an extraordinary year. And on the battlefield of domestic corporate public relations and marketing, it could be described as a bloodbath. For corporate marketing and public relations personnel, it seemed as if \"PR crises\" descended upon them like fierce beasts overnight, leaving people trembling with fear. Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, we are about to enter 2009. Looking back on this year, perhaps many business owners still have lingering fears and feel as if they are treading on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Leo friends at work almost never refuse any request; as long as they can showcase their talents and abilities, they will grit their teeth and help out. But as a result, they naturally tend to forget things, and the accumulated workload on their hands is considerable. Therefore, a readily prepared calendar and weekly planner are the most suitable office lucky charms for them, especially those with a lively and playful style, which perfectly matches their childlike nature. Even when extremely busy, they can easily solve problems."}
{"trans": "An excellent essay should include six or seven high-quality sentences: first, vivid and beautiful metaphorical sentences; second, magnificent parallel sentences; third, emotionally rich personification sentences; fourth, profound allusion sentences; fifth, enlightening philosophical sentences; sixth, mutually reinforcing contrast sentences; and seventh, agile and beautiful poetic sentences. Making good use of these high-quality sentences makes the writing concise yet profound, serves as the finishing touch that illuminates the entire essay, achieves great effect with little, and greatly enhances its literary quality."}
{"trans": "What's even more ridiculous is that nowadays, Western countries' economies remain at a loss, their printing presses are ready to roll, their finances are running on empty, yet they expect China to \"feed\" the world... Everyone is now turning their attention to China, the world's second-largest economy. If the post-Cold War global system dominated by the United States is on its last legs, will this emerging economic superpower step forward? Or will it let the West suffer the consequences of its own actions? But this time, China might be willing but unable!"}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for fifty-four years, expanding the territory to form a vast domain that stretched from central Korea in the east to the vicinity of Lake Balkhash in the west, from the heartland of Vietnam in the south to the Sayan Mountains in Outer Mongolia in the north. The population under his rule reached nearly sixty million. To be fair, among the hundreds of emperors in Chinese history, very few could expand the territory like Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che. It was considered good enough for the others to just preserve the empire without being prodigal sons who brought humiliation to the nation and forfeited its sovereignty. In this sense alone, Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, should be regarded as an emperor of great vision and strategic wisdom."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the trivial matters of ordinary people's lives, lacking twists and turns in the plot, but they give people a refreshing feeling due to their unique perspective and undeniable personal inclinations. He excels at creating distinctive, individualized characters, which is precisely the characteristic of a genius writer."}
{"trans": "Some people bluff and make exaggerated claims, constantly seeking selling points by positioning themselves as \"industry first\" or \"the first company\", packaging themselves and tirelessly promoting and marketing themselves in the flood of information; others, with the mindset of not displaying their wealth, focusing on self-improvement, hiding their capabilities and biding their time, accumulating strength before making a move, quietly work without making a sound."}
{"trans": "Actually, why do \"flame wars\" always spread everywhere and continue for months without stopping? What forces are fueling this from behind? What exactly is imperceptibly influencing netizens' judgments and thoughts? Not only ordinary netizens, but even some website administrators are also greatly puzzled by this."}
{"trans": "In the evening, he spread out the manuscript paper, preparing to write an article to earn back that 20 yuan. This evening, the title of his article was: \"On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality?\" He said: In this decadent era of material desire, we must hold high the banner of morality to oppose material enslavement. This evening, his essay advanced triumphantly, passionate, sad and indignant, heartbroken and filled with indignation, patient and systematic in its guidance, with boiling blood, heart-wrenching, showing utter devotion, sharp and unrestrained, smooth and soaring, flowing down a thousand miles..."}
{"trans": "1. Shen Lun requires foresight and a long-term perspective. As a type of official document, the most basic characteristic of Shen Lun is that its concept and theme must be elevated. Shen Lun writing should focus on long-term interests, see through appearances to the essence, be good at taking a commanding view, and be skilled at elevating the theme. In other words, the written essay must possess a noble ideological realm, must not pander to vulgar tastes, and certainly cannot be lowbrow, crude, or full of complaints."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is a compassion shown to those who suffer. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of people who seek the unknown, like stardust falling on children's eyelids, and also like a piece of bread in the throat."}
{"trans": "Look up further, how well-proportioned her shoulders are! Like twin lambs, or like two jade peaks; exactly as slender as autumn mountains, as smooth as autumn waters. Above the shoulders, we reach the face that is generally praised and celebrated."}
{"trans": "Even lotus flowers have the tragedy of the extermination of nine generations. Lotus after lotus connected, the thousand fingers of lotus petals held one summer, then released another summer. Now is the ghostly rain of an autumn night, splashing down on the water surface of broken duckweed, like a disheveled and blind Chopin abusing a thousand-keyed piano."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen teachings under the moon makes the meaning more profound; discussing swordsmanship under the moon makes one's spirit more authentic; discussing poetry under the moon enhances the elegance and subtlety; being with a beautiful person under the moon deepens affection. The way to appreciate the moon: When it's bright and clear, it's best to look up; when it's hazy, it's better to look down. The spring wind is like wine; the summer wind is like tea; the autumn wind is like smoke; the winter wind is like ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He rides the waves of blood, in a small red boat, gracefully arriving in this damp and cold world. His final leap was shot out of the gate of life by rolling heat waves, like the mud and sand all coming down when a flood breaks out. The baby's excited cries are like glass cups colliding and shattering."}
{"trans": "If China were to have one more gloomy writer, this north-facing study should be held responsible. Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a fruit pregnant with the south, refrigerated in a freezer. During the daytime, I seem to be submerged at the bottom of the sea, where the silent darkness plays gray music."}
{"trans": "The red candle has a spiritual nature; she doesn't begrudge her life, yet she is exceptionally attached to it. Every time when she is about to burn out, the scorched wick unexpectedly rises high and spasmodically like a spine in the flames, holding on, resembling a warrior suddenly hit by a bullet freezing in mid-air into a sculpture of defiance, and then heavily falling into a crimson pool of blood..."}
{"trans": "Looking out at the sky, its pattern prompts self-reflection. After morning dew and rain, the sun emerges, with silver droplets adorning everything, all shining brightly—one sun giving birth to countless suns. The old spiderweb in the corner need not be swept away; let dust gather upon it, and over time its threads will thicken like the roots of an old tree, forming a three-dimensional mural. From it, one can read tradition and modernity, finding new insights with each viewing."}
{"trans": "Spring always knocks on the bamboo gate of the garden first, and then lights up the extinguished torches from last year, one by one. At this time, winter, which has been guarding the empty house alone, is like a mournful wolf, abandoning its position and fleeing in the sudden flames. The flames make its lonely gaze at a loss, and the flowery skirt of the earth makes it lose its way."}
{"trans": "The methods of punishing evil are more evil than evil itself; the indiscriminate killing of innocents is as easy as cutting leeks. Under the banner of loyalty, filial piety, virtue, and righteousness, there is only the glint of swords and the flash of blades; the price of grandeur and magnificence is a field strewn with corpses. The fundamental value of life is a few withered stalks under horse hooves; the right of the common people to survive is but a few bubbles on the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "The sound of nature, the mystery of the infinite, the infinite's siege of the finite, or God's stern yet gentle command. Music is the omniscient and omnipotent God of musical notes; He is both the Creator—who arranges and defines the positions of the notes—and the Savior—if the notes can listen to and follow that unceasing and relentless performance."}
{"trans": "Above the winding lotus pond, what meets the eye is a field of lush leaves. The leaves rise high out of the water, like the skirts of graceful dancers. Among the layers of leaves, white flowers are scattered about, some blooming gracefully, others shyly in bud; just like bright pearls, or stars in the azure sky, or beauties just out of their bath."}
{"trans": "Therefore, as for cities, if everything one encounters and sees is young and beautiful, then it must be that the proper development has not been reached and the strings are not in harmony. This is like writing; when adjectives are like a woman in heavy makeup and parallel structures are like lovers walking side by side, then one has certainly not yet entered the true path of writing. The pinnacle of writing is like sparse paulownia trees on an old street, old seats under the trees, casual conversations among the seats - exquisite yet leisurely."}
{"trans": "The suffering of one household does not affect the world's happiness. Summer arrives irresistibly, and the albizia flowers, like pink powder puffs, brush against the lonely and desolate windowsill of the hospital room. The girl's head has become polygonal; the long-healed cranial sutures, like cracked earth, have opened into black holes under her thin skin, as an inner demon expands in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I am like a southern fruit full of ripeness, refrigerated in a freezer. During the day, I seem to be submerged at the bottom of the sea, where the silent darkness plays gray music. At night, I seem to hear the sound of Eskimo sleds gliding, while the long beard of the North Star hangs down, jingling and striking strings of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They are as quiet as the bright moon, not wanting to disturb anyone, yet they genuinely startled a wide area around them. This can truly be described as \"the moon rising startles the mountain birds.\" Compared to Tao Yuanming's quietness, Wang Wei's quietness has more of an aristocratic air and more of an exquisite design. His brilliance lies in being more common than the common people despite being aristocratic, and being more natural than nature itself despite being designed."}
{"trans": "Even the brown tea table was painted with emotion, a gentle little rectangle bearing all the liveliness above it. In another larger painting, there are also white magnolias, thin and bright, like jade or crystal, like the cool taste of the jade fish held in Yang Guifei's mouth when she had a toothache. The tough lines of the winter jasmine open and close with force; its control over life is both calm and domineering."}
{"trans": "\"Vast and boundless, I return to the great wilderness!\" Reading this passage, what I felt was not sadness, but beauty. That feeling was just like reading in 'Records of the Grand Historian' about Jing Ke in white clothes crossing the Yi River to assassinate the King of Qin, full of color. Imagine, a young master from a wealthy family who has seen through the worldly affairs, with a shaved head and bare feet, wearing a red cloak, standing in the snow to bid farewell to his father - what beauty!"}
{"trans": "We cannot bypass that dark, humiliating, and indifferent Chengde era, just as when approaching the Mogao Caves, we cannot but face that ugly and desolate Taoist pagoda. No matter how splendid and magnificent Dunhuang is in memory, it ultimately cannot fill the vast Library Cave, cannot wash away the pallor in the Thousand Buddha Caves, and cannot soothe the bleeding wounds of the ancient nation on the horizon."}
{"trans": "Forgetting visits us more and more frequently and becomes a faithful friend until death. I then use this friend to filter; what is forgotten is naturally unnecessary to remember. The subconscious manipulates memory, like the wind guiding a kite on an invisible level. New powerful threads weave into an uneven sieve of memory, and the remaining clots are like cheese, containing hard bits that hurt the teeth amidst the sweetness."}
{"trans": "His chest is majestic and upright, containing the heaven-shaking, earth-splitting roars of his ancestors chasing fierce beasts. His pelvis curves sharply inward, with the sharply protruding bones indicating that powerful muscle groups once attached here, like the ropes of Yellow River trackers, pulling the entire body in gecko-like climbing. And his limbs, like the slender and beautiful ivory of African elephants, emit a smooth, lustrous sheen like congealed fat."}
{"trans": "It was not until several years later that I dispelled my lingering resentment and admitted that day was a treacherous turn in my life. What prompted me to destroy that withered rose painting was not the art teacher's ridicule, but rather seeing your talent so brilliant and dazzling, which led me to break my paintbrush myself with a gesture of regret. What is regret like? It's like a small mole on one's body, only you yourself know its location and the process of its emergence."}
{"trans": "I was combing my hair on the balcony, and my hair fell like falling leaves, coming down in gusts, draping over my arms like night rain. From far and near, many car horns sounded in panic; the gradually darkening sky spread out on all sides like a vast lake of mist and rosy clouds. From a window on the ground floor of a house across the way, a wisp of pale cooking smoke rose hesitantly, as if not quite sure where the sky was."}
{"trans": "She carried a water kettle in each hand, which made me think of a woman walking with full spirit on a thin rope. This was all due to her waist; her waist, her waist was really too soft. In Baishui's words, it was so soft that it made me feel as if I were eating Suzhou's ox-hide candy. Not just her waist, as I wrote well in my diary: she had a set of curves that could compete in beauty with clouds and rosy clouds, and contend in spirit with the moon in water, weaving into a large, bewitching net!"}
{"trans": "\"Because of your language, you fall silent, and when sinking to the deepest point, you let yourself disappear.\" Losing language, thus losing the self, losing the entity of existence, Yang Lian therefore recognizes that he has become a \"ghost\"; a ghost, floating between cities, observing with cold detachment (like an insect, a ghost is also an \"it\", only able to observe), observing the complete annihilation of this thing called \"meaning\". There is a sea, yet the harbor has no meaning for you."}
{"trans": "Each streetlight is far apart from the next. Between stretches of brightness are stretches of darkness. My shadow appears in the brightness and disappears in the darkness. The wind, coming from nowhere, ripples the colorful fallen leaves, as if stirring up impressions of life. I feel like this empty wind, only able to capture my own existence when it causes the colorful fallen leaves to drop and swirl."}
{"trans": "But we standing on the open land—my father, brother, relatives, and many fellow villagers who had shed blood and sweat, been scorched by the sun, and drenched by wind and rain—stood frozen listening to the distant thunder, with no one appearing to want to go inside to escape the northwest rain. Our hearts were more gloomy than the sky, everyone was silent, because our hearts were also a sky about to rain, and this heart-rain seemed more tragic and more pouring down than the northwest rain."}
{"trans": "Imagine if Tang Bohu and Qianlong were both considered \"first-rate poets of ancient China,\" then we could only quietly burn the entire \"Complete Tang Poems.\" The same is true for calligraphy. When an astonishing sky-high price is placed on a piece of mediocre calligraphy, it's like a pile of gold crushing the balance of Chinese calligraphy history. Faced with this situation, I once sighed deeply: \"When the cultural lineage is hidden, small hills are called peaks; when the strong wings are far away, broken feathers fill the role of the great bird.\""}
{"trans": "The seizure happened very suddenly, as if the girl had received a decree descending from the sky, convulsing abruptly without any warning. The soft girl shriveled like an extremely hard rolling pin, every muscle glistening like iron. Her small body was like a curved bow for shooting eagles, bouncing on the sickly white hospital bed. Countless drops of sweat from this grotesque human rainbow bridge dripped and splattered, like the eaves of a snow-covered house during the warm spring when flowers bloom."}
{"trans": "This unleashed force, solitary yet powerful, both following and breaking conventions, combining intoxication with poetry, resembles the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu treated his brush as if staggering in drunken steps, swaying, dancing with hands and feet, with an elegant posture, energetically completing all movements in one fluid motion, then throwing down his cup and laughing, and falling into a sound sleep. Zhang Xu did not know that his drunken steps were precisely the steps of Tang Dynasty culture."}
{"trans": "But when I was holding my breath and listening attentively, they suddenly and simultaneously fell silent. These cicadas startled me again! Like a rope, the sound of cicadas had tightly bound my heart, and then suddenly, without warning, it loosened. So my heart, unprepared, scattered apart, like a wave forcefully leaping toward the sky only to accidentally fall onto the beach! When did summer cross the threshold and arrive? I didn't even know!"}
{"trans": "I once shed tears for your humiliation and disappointment. My tears flowed like streams, clear as crystal, yet they could not wash away your thick filth; they only removed the veil from my eyes. These tears could not moisten your hearts of stone in the slightest, but only extinguished the anxious and eager flames in my heart. Now, at your suffering, I laugh, and this laughter is like thunder—it does not come after the storm, but roars before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually understood that when facing disaster, one cannot use the grammar of disaster; there is another grammar that leads directly to the poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From this point on, my state of life was no longer the same. Every time I read chapters of Zhuangzi such as 'Autumn Floods,' 'Free and Easy Wandering,' 'Discussion on Making All Things Equal,' and 'The World,' it was like looking at electrocardiograms related to me. For such a closely related ancient philosopher, it is difficult for me to make calm and fair evaluations, so I can only avoid doing so."}
{"trans": "You press your forehead against the gold-embroidered fabric. When the sun was on this side, it made the gold threads scorching hot, but now it's cold. The people of the past struggled through their lives, and what they did gradually became covered in dust; when their descendants hang out clothes to dry, they shake off the dust again, dancing in the yellow sun. If memory had a scent, it would be the fragrance of camphor, sweet and secure, like a distinctly remembered happiness, sweet and sorrowful, like forgotten sorrow."}
{"trans": "It is this quality that brings them close to life, allowing us, even a thousand years later, to feel close to them. Yang Guifei's vibrancy, I think, is like a ceramic thermos, warm and smooth as jade, placed at one's feet. As the water inside gradually cools, it gives one a feeling of gentle persistence. Su Qing, however, is like a small red clay stove, with its own independent fire. You can see the red flames and hear the crackling sounds, but it is rather difficult to tend to, requiring coal and firewood to be added, with choking smoke."}
{"trans": "Like surging waves and like terrifying tides, they beat against the emotions settled at the bottom of your heart. In an instant, you feel that the sound of cicadas, like fierce waves washing away sand, snatches away the light sorrow you were clutching tightly in your hands. The urgency of the cicada's song suddenly stops at its highest note, even more like a magnificent article being violently torn apart, with sonorous words scattered all over the ground, landing with the sound of metal and stone, and then becoming silent and sparse, a fragmentary text, leaving only some melancholy and some sadness. Is this not also a song of life?"}
{"trans": "Here there is vibrant youth, here there are hot, fiery hearts; there are no decadent little old people, only vigorous old youths. The silvery white moon wanders in the empty sky, she seems to be shedding tears, she hates her loneliness.... And then there is that swimming pool, always like a kind old grandmother, smiling with a face full of wrinkles, when she sees many lively children plopping into the water like little mermaids, she bursts with joy, creating great splashes of silver water."}
{"trans": "For thousands of years, it has been a lost wilderness. Beyond the wilderness are indistinct, anonymous great craftsmen, while on this side is a panicking contemporary woman. On both sides, the kiln fires burn fiercely, like two beacon towers separated by thousands of mountains and rivers, yet the signals they transmit are precise and unmistakable. All other beacon towers are related to war, but these two are not. Separated by the bloodshed of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang dynasties, and the battles of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, there are only two wisps of the purest smoke, echoing each other from afar."}
{"trans": "Lin Daiyu's brokenness lies in her unforgettable love; Sanmao's brokenness stems from her moment of clarity and transcendence after experiencing all the vicissitudes of life; Van Gogh's brokenness is the sun using golden knives to make him suffer intensely in the light; Beethoven's brokenness is the tragic movement of life created by the collision of the most spiritual black and white keys. If the brokenness of ordinary people reveals the purest and most beautiful spark of human nature, then the brokenness of these outstanding souls is like silver fireworks filling the sky above our heads."}
{"trans": "The face is washed several times a day, but it's still not clean. The eyes are never washed in a lifetime, yet they remain bright forever. There's no spare space to use mops and brooms, so there's no need to spend that money. After all, people are mobile and are naturally dust-repelling pearls. Strangely, the air doesn't become thin due to the cramped space. To make human breathing visible, cigarette smoke serves as tangible air. One breath is taken in, three are exhaled, curling and rising to the ceiling. Shrouded in auspicious clouds, one can first observe the abundance of all things below, and then look up to contemplate the vastness of the universe."}
{"trans": "To know oneself but not to know others is merely a method of confining oneself to a corner, never interacting with others; it is nothing more than being like a summer insect that cannot speak of ice, a frog at the bottom of a well, or a donkey in a mill. Only by knowing others can one truly have self-knowledge; just like Princess Iron Fan's fan, one must be able to release in order to gather. The more one knows, the wider one's connections; by scattering oneself throughout the world, permeating into all things to observe their dimensions, shapes, weights, and densities, only then can one gradually recognize one's true self with the precision of dissecting the finest details."}
{"trans": "The singing voice flows like clouds and water, allowing one to cast aside worries and wander leisurely within it. Also like surging waves and terrifying billows, it beats against the emotions settled at the bottom of your heart. In an instant, you feel that the cicada's sound, like fierce waves sifting sand, snatches away the light sorrow you tightly hold in your hands. The urgency of the cicada's sound suddenly stops at the highest note, even more like a splendid essay suddenly torn apart, scattering resonant phrases all over the ground that fall with the sound of metal and stone. Then it becomes silent and lonely, turning into fragmented passages, only leaving people with some melancholy and some sadness."}
{"trans": "What nihilism is there? The affairs of God are unknown to humans; human's affair is to construct and continue meaning amidst the siege of fate—or one could say helplessly—thereby saving the present and also saving eternity. Therefore, 'eternal recurrence' is by no means 'a comprehensive affirmation of earthly life,' but merely means: humans cannot escape earthly life, not even in death. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence toward eternity, that is, the earth's gaze toward the heavens—that grand piece of music has always filled heaven and earth."}
{"trans": "Looking at Master Xiaoyun's Zen paintings, the experience is completely different. That feeling is as if we are reading the pastoral poems of Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei in the middle of the night. With just a few strokes and light ink, they do not stir up turbulent emotions in our souls; instead, they calm our turbulence. It does not stuff something into our hearts, but rather washes away the worldly concerns that originally fill our minds, just like a mountain stream after a heavy rain. The stream water is initially muddy, but when the rain clears and the sky turns blue, the stream becomes completely clear, and the mud and filth in the mountains are also washed away clean."}
{"trans": "This sound was sometimes slow, sometimes urgent; sometimes high, sometimes low; sometimes loud, sometimes deep; sometimes intermittent, sometimes continuous. At times it was like the chime of gold and jade, at times like the great bells of ancient music, at times like large and small pearls falling on a jade plate, at times like red corals and white pearls sinking into the sea, at times like playing an unadorned zither, at times like dancing thunderbolts, at times like a hundred birds contending in song, at times like a rabbit falling and a hawk rising. My thoughts wandered freely, beyond my control, my heart blossomed with joy, and inspiration flowed from my pen. The dead words seemed to come alive, and I seemed to be filled once more with youthful vitality. Rarely in my life have I experienced such a spiritual state, and it is even more difficult to convey it to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps, clouds were meant to travel in the sky; unlike the sun with its fiery wheel-like feet, they won't descend to receive my warm hospitality. It's merely my illusion, but what a beautiful illusion it is. If the blue sky is a wordless celestial book, then clouds must be its unannotated footnotes, and the rapid tracks of my car translating the language of clouds onto the road surface are the newly published commentary. The sky unfolds with its changing blue, the clouds are depicted with pure strokes, and then handed to my eyes to print. We are all narrating the story of Kuafu."}
{"trans": "It was inconvenient to take it out and eat on the plane. When I got back to America and tasted it, it was too oily and too spicy, nothing like the sausage rolls I occasionally ate from my father. In Shanghai, next to our house was the Kiessling Cafe, which had newly moved from Tianjin during the war. Every day at dawn, they made bread, setting off an olfactory alarm. A rich, fragrant aroma would fill the air with the force of a ten-thousand-mile wind, yet it was the softest of alarm clocks. However, it woke people up at the wrong time, as frustrating as the annoying beauty of spring that leaves one helpless. Having this 'fragrant' neighbor was truly a disturbance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like the sugar that coax children to take medicine, or even more like the electric rabbit that entices dogs to race in a dog track. A few minutes or days of happiness make us live a lifetime, enduring much pain. We hope for it to come, hope for it to stay, hope for it to come again—these three sentences summarize the entire history of human endeavor. While we pursue and wait, life stealthily slips away unnoticed. Perhaps we are merely the chips consumed by time, living a lifetime only to serve as sacrificial offerings to the years of that lifetime, never even thinking of happiness."}
{"trans": "There was a dark olive-green silk, with large black shadows sweeping across it, filled with wind and thunder. There was also a Japanese silk material, light lake-colored, shimmering with wood grain and water ripples; every so often, two plum blossoms the size of teacups floated on the water, with iron strokes and silver hooks, like the stained glass windows in medieval chapels, red glass embedded with heavy iron borders. The most common on the market were various nameless colors, not quite blue, not quite gray, not quite yellow, that could only serve as backgrounds; these were all neutral colors, also called protective colors, civilized colors, or mixed colors."}
{"trans": "This comes from her movements; her every step, stretch of her waist, brush of her hair, turn of her eyes, lowering of her head, and even the slight flutter of her sleeves and gentle dance of her skirt are all like the flow of honey, the gentle ripple of wind; how could we not be filled with joy and admiration? The most lovely is that soft waist; people of the past spoke of willows bending in the wind, and in 'Dream of the Red Chamber' Qingwen's water-snake waist, both describing the slender softness of the waist; but the waist that I love is simply like Suzhou's cowhide candy, making my whole tongue sweet and my teeth soft. With a waist so soft, her hands and feet naturally have an extraordinary grace."}
{"trans": "Beside, some wine bottles leaned askew, with little wine left in them. Unfortunately, I don't drink; otherwise, at a moment like this, taking a few sips would surely be a wonderful delight. \"Raising my cup, I invite the bright moon,\" and the moon would shyly slip into your cup. A gentle breeze passes by, and you can hear the forests on the mountains on both sides rustling. In the swaying of the branches, the lights flicker in and out of sight, just like mischievous children playing hide-and-seek with you. Coordinating with the leaping, scale-like light on the river's surface, it's as if they're jointly performing an enchanting melody. What kind of earthly dream is this?"}
{"trans": "I can no longer explain clearly how there can be such a sense of desolation on the stage illuminated by real sunlight. Between art and reality, there is a place where they overlap, becoming hazy and indistinct; it's like holding a matchstick burning in the sunlight, flickering and wavering, where the pale orange-yellow flame can barely be seen, but one can feel more distinctly one's own hand, also a temporary thing in the sunlight... The maid on stage sang for a while, holding a tea tray, moving through rooms with a graceful gesture like parting flowers and brushing willows, crossing countless thresholds, arriving at the study, bowing to the young master, and raising the tea tray level with her eyebrows."}
{"trans": "I saw a calico cat lying diagonally under a dilapidated, abandoned broken wall, with morning glories blooming in a rich mix of deep green and vibrant purple, and the cat stretched lazily without a care. In the hazy night, I saw the streetlights casting the shadow of a power box on the sidewalk haphazardly onto a white wall at a construction site, interweaving with the swaying shadows of roadside trees in a play of light and dark, looking just like the balcony where Romeo sang love songs to Juliet. I saw the face of poet Zhou Mengdie, as I waved goodbye to him, perfectly framed in the small window of a moving bus, as if the entire vehicle were solemnly serving as his picture frame."}
{"trans": "You think of that childlike heart, naked yet desiring and loving everything, visibly fading in the faint morning mist; no matter how you wave your hand, it never returns to your bosom. How incomplete this feels! So Mr. Pingbo, feeling suffocated, honestly and sincerely, like a gentle spring breeze whispering among green trees, softly and intimately tells you of his memorable yet elusive \"childhood.\" Although he cannot live in that \"childhood\" forever, if he can invite a few more companions to wander there for a while, he can somewhat alleviate his sense of emptiness, and that taste of melancholy will not always linger on his tongue."}
{"trans": "You could also say that it is the starting point for the Chinese people's march toward modernity, but which nation's steps toward modernity would be as hurried, flustered, timid, and disorganized as Shanghai's? You could also say that it is an urban civilization that rose in opposition to agricultural civilization, but what kind of urban civilization would, like Shanghai, always be deeply coveted, decomposed, surrounded, and shrouded by the vast power of the countryside? In short, it is a huge paradox; when you gaze upon its foulness, it rises with dazzling brightness, and when you worship its great power, it turns around to show you its scar-studded back wall."}
{"trans": "However, the truth is just the opposite. I sat there quietly, listening to the sound of raindrops above my head. At this moment, having sound was better than silence. I felt immeasurable joy in my heart, as if I had drunk immortal dew and absorbed pure enlightenment, feeling as if I were about to ascend to immortality. This sound was sometimes slow and sometimes urgent, sometimes high and sometimes low, sometimes loud and sometimes deep, sometimes intermittent and sometimes continuous. Sometimes it was like the resonance of gold and jade, sometimes like the great bells of ancient times, sometimes like large and small pearls falling on a jade plate, sometimes like red corals and white pearls sinking into the sea, sometimes like playing an elegant zither, sometimes like dancing thunderbolts, sometimes like a hundred birds contending in song, sometimes like a rabbit falling and a hawk rising. My thoughts wandered freely, beyond my control, my heart blossomed with joy, and inspiration flowed from my pen."}
{"trans": "Around him were many colorful billboards and shops, with car horns beeping; He was like the person in the ancient legend who had the Yellow Millet Dream, except he had merely woken up from a sleep without experiencing such a dream—with an even greater sense of pity. The Taoist priest walked to the front of a hardware store and prostrated himself, of course, the people inside didn't give him money, and he, acting as if no one was around, just kowtowed dazedly and left it at that. He got up by himself, tapping 'to—to—', and moved to the entrance of the tobacco and paper shop next door, once again 'kneeling down in the dust', with his head hanging crookedly, his movements were like a black eddy, like a black chrysanthemum slowly blooming."}
{"trans": "What of it? Birds sing in spring, crickets chirp in autumn, mosquitoes buzz like thunder in summer, and at night insects awaken while birds sleep. Wind and rain don't occur every day, dogs don't bark without visitors, and hens don't crow without laying eggs. Only humans use language, gestures, and machines to make sounds anytime, anywhere. Even when alone in a room with no one to respond to, they can turn on a gramophone, listen to the radio, or even produce thunder-like snores while sleeping. Language is certainly not just sound, but in the case of unpleasant, unwanted, or indistinct language heard through walls or from a distance, words lose their edges and contours, becoming a mass of swelling and shrinking clamor, as meaningless as a hen's crow or a dog's bark."}
{"trans": "As time passes, the past is forever gone, impossible to turn back to that first moment of encountering peach blossoms by a face; yet in human memory, the charm or lingering wounds of the past often surge back like waves lapping the shore, making the present an extension of the past's charm or lingering wounds, continuing further and farther, endlessly growing. If life is a pre-bound, pre-paged blank book, then the disturbances of past events on a person are like writing too heavily on a certain page, with ink seeping through to the following pages, impossible to erase. Of course, there's no need to destroy old pages for satisfaction, just as the yellow crane has already flown away, why destroy the Yellow Crane Tower; however, it is necessary to spread out the old history under the lamp, going where one should go and stopping where one should stop."}
{"trans": "The Great Northwest is a land of barren basalt mountains where not a blade of grass grows, of great deserts with lone plumes of smoke rising straight up. You are a geologist, with a large canvas geological bag slung over your shoulder, and you have been rushing about for twenty years. Your tent of twenty years, in the sea of sand mountains, is like a small boat. The cold crescent moon shines down. Can the bell of Hanshan Temple outside Suzhou city reach the passenger boat at midnight? Your wife, that beauty as lovely as flowers and jade, is gazing at you. Her face is covered with a net of longing, as she tries to catch a heart of love that has gone far away. You go back once a year, and each time you plant a clump of bamboo in front of the door. But then you leave again, leaving her with clusters of bamboo leaves that form the character \"ge\"."}
{"trans": "If life is a blank book, pre-bound and pre-paginated, the disturbances of past affairs on a person are like writing too heavily on a certain page, where the ink stains seep through to the following pages, impossible to erase. Of course, there's no need to destroy the old pages for satisfaction, just as the yellow crane has already flown away, why destroy the Yellow Crane Tower; however, it is necessary to spread out the old history under the lamp, going where one should go and stopping where one should stop. After embracing life completely, one can look at old matters or new things with great tolerance, giving them their deserved position and meaning. If it is a beautiful thing, one can see what kind of branches sprout from its bud; if it is a sad thing, one also sees a tender branch stretching from a cloudy day toward a sunny one."}
{"trans": "Everything is distant from me, even my own shadow in the bright moon appears hazier than smoke. I was just about to turn around to sleep; for some reason, I hesitated with a step, and the fleeting dream suddenly paused, though it immediately flew away like an arrow released from its bow."}
{"trans": "The last hope is merely an aesthetic support. Just like a ship sinking in the icy sea, completely beyond rescue, looking up at the scene of rolling dark clouds; just like under chaotic blade attacks with absolutely no way to survive, looking down at the pattern of splashing blood. Aesthetic support is the final support."}
{"trans": "What we gather from the past and future are just tiny seeds. When you are a wish wandering in the mist, I too wander in it. We seek each other, dreams grow from our longing, those dreams are continuous and boundless."}
{"trans": "In such purity, the dish is oneself, the cook is oneself, and the eater is still oneself. Just as love is oneself, the one who knows this love is oneself, and the one who recalls this love is still oneself. Savoring oneself bite by bite, through the cup of time, one intoxicates oneself."}
{"trans": "The trousers cling tightly, unable to take a step. My mind is as simple as a piece of paper, as blank as a newborn baby. Saying goodbye to the sea, saying goodbye to a lonely seabird circling in the sky. I will come again, to speak of the dust of the eight wildernesses and nine heavens. Picking up the umbrella and shoes, picking up the various things of the human world."}
{"trans": "Unpredictable. I only hope that, even as a human failing, it should present itself with proper dignity. Like the frown and sigh of a noble warrior, rather than the midnight brawl of a group of ragged soldiers; like the millennial confrontation of two snow peaks, rather than a tangle of vines wrapping around a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night on the plateau was exceptionally beautiful. The sky resembled a blue ritual vessel fired during the Jingtai era of the Ming Dynasty—deep and boundless. Through the enormous moon, like a silver table, one could still see the metallic blue light behind it. The moonlight was no match for the blue sky's dyeing, drifting like diluted ink, thread by thread."}
{"trans": "Repeatedly watching the same movie is like vomiting out eaten food and chewing it again. In that instant, the tops of our heads turned golden, as if covered with the awns of wheat. I recalled a character in Gorky's books once said that young lovers should not meet again later in life, like a skeleton standing up from the ground..."}
{"trans": "When I close my eyes, I think of it; when I open my eyes, I want it. And when all of this comes rushing at me, almost about to overwhelm me, I simply don't know what I want anymore. I only feel my heart aching persistently, like being tightly bound by silken threads, like being scalded by drops of candle wax, like being tossed about on the vast sea."}
{"trans": "The echo of your slightest sobs will become it. After life is veiled, it, like your greatest souls, is covered and hidden. When life speaks, all winds turn into words; when life speaks again, the smile on your lips, the tears in your eyes, will also turn into words."}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality has grown increasingly dim. Spring gives way to autumn, plum blossoms wither and cranes grow old; culture has become a purposeless waste, and closed-minded moral perfection has led to overall immorality. The advancement of civilization has thus been cancelled, leaving behind a pile of plum petals and crane feathers, like bookmarks tucked into the annals of the national spirit."}
{"trans": "To grant a pass to the religious spirit based on the standards of science and philosophy is like using intellect and reasoning to pursue love; it will inevitably suppress the passion of life and exhaust the charm of love. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is like treating family status and property as conditions for marriage, turning children into reproductive machines and making them spiritual eunuchs."}
{"trans": "Actually, all destruction is concrete, all grievances are difficult to express, and therefore those answers are also questionable. What need not be doubted is the result, withered grass and rubble carrying the disasters one by one from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face all of this in a perilous situation without any protection mechanism, just like taking off gloves to caress the scars of an elderly person."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written so many pages. I see myself like a child, copying a passage from a long hymn; the angels had sung that hymn when God shaped the first man. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person, memorizing a sentence from a book written by wisdom; that book was written on the title page of emotions before time appeared."}
{"trans": "Even if they are great events spanning a thousand years, or grand feats connecting vast distances, if they belong to culture, they are often borne by a pair of aging shoulders. Like smugglers, like fugitives, dodging and making secret inquiries along the way, seeking a place to entrust. The decision to entrust is always written in a will, thus making it impossible to elucidate the cultural meaning of one's own life while alive."}
{"trans": "Undoubtedly, the result is withered grass and rubble, bearing one disaster after another from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face all this in a perilous situation without any protective mechanism, just like taking off gloves to touch the wounds of an elderly person. This touching often triggers deep contemplation: As the foundation of our lives, Chinese civilization is also full of scars, yet how did it avoid a complete collapse?"}
{"trans": "Could anyone possibly hand you a pre-made meaning along with your birth certificate? Being born is, in itself, a demand for meaning from the one who is born - it requires you to find or create meaning, much like a publishing contract with an advance payment that lasts a lifetime. Of course, you are not the creditor but the debtor; it is life that demands meaning from you, and you have no right to complain about anyone."}
{"trans": "Those uneven inks, those red-tinted headlines, those crossed-out names, those rows of exclamation marks, those restrained appeals, those repeated revisions - they all combined into a terrifying sound, rushing toward me. This is like how just a few white hairs in a spiderweb in the corner of a room, or a half piece of rag among the withered leaves on a treetop, can immediately transport us to that era we dare not think of."}
{"trans": "Some fell on the hair buns of vegetable-picking women, some stuck to the black coats of swallows, and some slid into the small river to play in the water. The river, like a thousand flute-playing vagrants, accompanies the joyful songs of schoolchildren. When mischievous children put their books on top of their yellow hats, holding two shoes to wade across the river, will spore babies pop out from the flute holes, bite onto the children's clothes, and finally return to the soil of their wild fern mothers?"}
{"trans": "Oh, soul, come back! Return to your old home. When he spoke Minnan dialect and made people laugh heartily, when he spoke Beijing dialect and made people look at each other in bewilderment, why didn't he defend himself: Here, his Chu accent is as profound as the heaven, earth, mountains, and rivers, as magnificent as the blue sky and ghosts and gods? Every sound of the emcee, like the sound of father reciting 'A Statement of My Situation', is melodious and sorrowful, every sound heavily wounds you."}
{"trans": "He was too thin, his withered skin couldn't fill the gaps between his ribs, so the pancake lay like a steel bridge across the ribcage. His violent and heavy heartbeat was like a bleeding sun, burning emptily, making the sounds of flames and caves. Mei Ying had heard Yue Beizhi's heartbeat, deep and low. Through his well-developed muscles, that heart beat like coal buried deep in the earth's crust, steadily and rhythmically."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, a person who has never settled in mountain villages or by watersides, what talisman can I pray for? Perhaps it is youth, but how fleeting it is. I am like someone who has discovered a treasure, carrying pearls, gold and silver in a leaky mesh bag, only to find that the journey becomes lighter and lighter, youth has scattered into dust. Perhaps it is scriptures and classics, but how can profound knowledge mend the broken mirror in my hands?"}
{"trans": "In the mountain hollows of my hometown, when greeting someone from far away, it's never the soft \"ai---\" of city dwellers, nor is it the feigned surprise \"wa---\" of southerners. The \"ai\" and \"wa\" can't travel far before being swallowed by the mountains. Only the deep, heavy, long, and desolate \"e-ha---\" soars like a golden eagle for a long time. Now, this eagle's cry falls like mist from the sky, and endless nostalgia, hot and spicy, fills Shen Zhanping's chest."}
{"trans": "Quickly escape from the political mire that even oneself doesn't understand at all, and chase after the long-lost poetic feeling. Chasing after poetic feeling is also chasing after oneself, the self that was once familiar to the land, held tightly by one's wife, the self that was thought to have been found but was instead lost. This time, turning back to chase, there is the morning glow to see one off, the river flow as witness, the cries of apes as encouragement, and ten thousand mountains making way. Therefore, the ship of life, which had become increasingly burdened, has once again become a light boat."}
{"trans": "Although airplanes can be imagined as Zhuangzi's carefree wandering or Liezi's journey riding the wind, they are not pleasing to watch for long. How can they compare to the long train rides, with their hypnotic rhythm and changing scenery? Looking out through the window, it feels as if you are both in the human world and beyond it. Therefore, when traveling abroad, wherever the clanging double tracks can reach, I always stand on the platform—a veritable \"long pavilion\"—waiting for the masculine beauty of the train rumbling unceasingly into the station to carry me to distant lands."}
{"trans": "Opposing prominence is the ordinary, opposing the officialdom is the common people. What has more power of concealment than the thatch and dense trees in the mountains and forests is disappearing into the ordinary life of common people in some small town. The concealment in the mountains and forests still preserves and displays a kind of aloof pride, and the concealment of aloof pride is ultimately insincere; the concealment in the small town streets not only doesn't need to deliberately torture and destroy life, but instead can make life very comfortable, allowing life to fit snugly in a corner that is both quiet and convenient, almost able to dissolve itself from outside to inside, thus becoming the highest form of concealment. To say 'concealment' may be too narrow, but in my mind anyway, the image of 'small bridges, flowing water, and households' and the 'longing for water shield and perch fish' are all ecological images of a religious life philosophy."}
{"trans": "The spring breeze does not know me, why does it enter my silk curtains?"}
{"trans": "From now on, I have no heart to love the beautiful nights, letting the bright moon set beyond the west tower."}
{"trans": "The candle has a heart and grieves our parting, shedding tears until dawn."}
{"trans": "Chang'e must regret stealing the elixir of immortality, alone in the vast blue sky and sea night after night with a lonely heart."}
{"trans": "Three times the lord sought your plans for the world,\nTwo dynasties you helped establish and support with the loyalty of an old servant."}
{"trans": "Strategic plans that carved the empire into three,\nA single feather in the eternal sky."}
{"trans": "A melody of 'The Backyard Flower', its deep sorrow too painful to hear."}
{"trans": "The swallows that once flew before the halls of Wang and Xie, now fly into the homes of ordinary people."}
{"trans": "Melancholy without reason to see Fan Li, jagged misty trees east of the Five Lakes."}
{"trans": "Had the east wind not favored Zhou Yu, in the deep spring of the Bronze Sparrow Terrace, the two Qiaos would have been locked away."}
{"trans": "Victory and defeat are unpredictable matters for military strategists; enduring humiliation and shame is what makes a real man."}
{"trans": "How does forty-eight years as emperor compare to the Lu family having Mo Chou?"}
{"trans": "Holding the tally, I bid farewell to the Phoenix Tower; Iron cavalry surround the Dragon City."}
{"trans": "Why must the Qiang flute resent the willows? The spring breeze does not reach Yumen Pass."}
{"trans": "Through hundreds of battles in the yellow sands, the golden armor is worn through; until Loulan is conquered, we will never return."}
{"trans": "The moon of Qin times, the passes of Han times,\nThe men of the ten-thousand-li march have not returned."}
{"trans": "Frontier guards gaze upon the border landscape, their faces sorrowful with thoughts of home."}
{"trans": "Shoot the man, first shoot the horse; capture the bandits, first capture their king."}
{"trans": "Across the vast desert, ice extends a hundred fathoms deep;\nGloomy clouds condense for ten thousand miles, dreary and bleak."}
{"trans": "In the dark woods, the grass trembles in the wind; the general draws his bow at night."}
{"trans": "In the great desert, sand lies like snow; above the Yan Mountains, the moon hangs like a hook."}
{"trans": "Hoeing crops at midday, sweat drips to the soil beneath."}
{"trans": "A horseman kicks up red dust, and the imperial concubine smiles; No one knows it's lychees that have arrived."}
{"trans": "My five-flower horse and thousand-gold fur coat, I'll have my son bring them out to exchange for fine wine, and together with you we'll drown our eternal sorrows."}
{"trans": "I wish to cross the Yellow River, but ice blocks the stream; I want to climb the Taihang Mountains, but snow fills the peaks."}
{"trans": "When the Emperor summons, I refuse to board the boat; I call myself the immortal of wine."}
{"trans": "Creation's masterworks all gather here,\nThe mountain cleaves the daylight from the dark."}
{"trans": "My lost soul cannot be called back, a rooster crows and the world turns white."}
{"trans": "Contemplating the vastness of the universe, alone I weep with sorrow."}
{"trans": "Endless falling leaves rustle down, the boundless Yangtze rolls on."}
{"trans": "Riding proudly on the swift horse in spring breeze; I've seen all the flowers of Chang'an in a single day."}
{"trans": "Zhuangzi in morning dream was fascinated by the butterfly; Emperor Wang entrusted his spring heart to the cuckoo."}
{"trans": "Vast desert, lone smoke straight; long river, setting sun round."}
{"trans": "Sitting alone in the secluded bamboo grove, playing the qin and also whistling loudly."}
{"trans": "The flying stream plunges down three thousand feet,\nI suspect it is the Milky Way falling from the nine heavens."}
{"trans": "The window frames the eternal snow on the western ridge; the door moors the ten-thousand-li boats from Eastern Wu."}
{"trans": "Scattered flowers gradually dazzle the eye, while shallow grass just covers the horse's hooves."}
{"trans": "Four hundred and eighty temples of the Southern Dynasties, how many towers and pavilions in the misty rain."}
{"trans": "During the Qingming Festival, the rain falls continuously. The pedestrians on the road seem to be in deep sorrow."}
{"trans": "I wonder who tailored the delicate leaves, the spring breeze in February is like scissors."}
{"trans": "In April on the plain all flowers have passed their prime,\nIn mountain temples peach blossoms just begin to bloom."}
{"trans": "A bosom friend afar brings a distant land near."}
{"trans": "If my kinsfolk in Luoyang ask about me, say my heart is like ice in a jade vessel."}
{"trans": "I urge you to finish one more cup of wine, for west of Yangguan Pass there will be no old friends."}
{"trans": "I entrust my sorrow to the bright moon, which will follow you to the west of Yelang."}
{"trans": "The Peach Blossom Pool is a thousand feet deep, yet not so deep as Wang Lun's love in seeing me off."}
{"trans": "The lone sail's distant shadow vanishes into the blue emptiness; I only see the Yangtze River flowing to the horizon."}
{"trans": "The verdant Bamboo Forest Temple, the faint evening bell sounds."}
{"trans": "Nearing home, my heart grows timid; I dare not ask the traveler."}
{"trans": "Hearing the willow-breaking song this night, who would not feel nostalgic for their homeland?"}
{"trans": "The beacon fires have burned for three months; a letter from home is worth ten thousand gold pieces."}
{"trans": "Who says that the heart of a little blade of grass can repay the kindness of the spring sun?"}
{"trans": "The flute's faint sound drifts through the reed flowers, white birds in formation suddenly startle and rise."}
{"trans": "The wave-rider stands at the crest of the waves, holding a red flag that remains dry."}
{"trans": "Verdant and countless, along roads in all directions."}
{"trans": "Beyond the misty green poplars, the morning chill is light; on the branches of red apricots, spring is in full bloom."}
{"trans": "Resting midway on a path of fragrant grass,\nIn late spring's cold, as rain clouds pass."}
{"trans": "The fragrance comes late on the gentle night breeze; by dawn, they bloom all over the southern branches."}
{"trans": "No need for light green or deep red, it is naturally the finest among flowers."}
{"trans": "If trees had feelings, they would not be so green!"}
{"trans": "Cold moon and dew, yellow parasol leaves drift."}
{"trans": "I still remember our parting on Jingshu Tower, under a moon bright as water."}
{"trans": "When the night is deep and wind still, as I prepare to leave, only a river of moonlight like jade-green glass remains."}
{"trans": "Dreams of my homeland's mountains and rivers are broken, separated by layers of misty waters."}
{"trans": "The lover's knot on the silk belt remains untied, while the tide at the riverbank has already ebbed."}
{"trans": "Thinking of the long journey ahead, a thousand li of misty waves, the evening mist hangs heavy over the vast Chu sky."}
{"trans": "With tearful eyes, I ask the flowers, but the flowers don't answer; scattered red petals fly past the swing."}
{"trans": "Falling flowers, a person stands alone; light rain, swallows fly in pairs."}
{"trans": "A lonely grave a thousand li away, nowhere to speak of the desolation."}
{"trans": "I miss you day after day, but I cannot see you; we drink from the same Yangtze River."}
{"trans": "Though our solemn vows still stand, this precious message I cannot send."}
{"trans": "The old events of the Six Dynasties flow away with the water, but only cold mist and withered grass remain, congealed in green."}
{"trans": "With a feather fan and a silk scarf, amidst casual conversation, the enemy fleet was reduced to ashes and smoke."}
{"trans": "Hearing several cranes calling at night, everyone says the king's army is approaching."}
{"trans": "To have a son, one should have someone like Sun Zhongmou!"}
{"trans": "Thirty years of fame and achievements are but dust and dirt; eight thousand miles of journey through clouds and moon."}
{"trans": "Under Fuli Temple, sacred crows and ceremonial drums fill the air."}
{"trans": "Returning drunk, I touch my sword and lean against the west wind; the river waves still inspire the human spirit."}
{"trans": "The river rushes like a whale, the mountain crouches like a tiger; this natural peril is not man-made."}
{"trans": "Fog obscures the towers, moonlight veils the ferry crossings."}
{"trans": "Flutes play in the sunshine, songs of water chestnut gatherers drift through the night, joyful are the old fishermen and the young lotus-picking maidens."}
{"trans": "In the fragrance of rice flowers, we speak of a bountiful harvest year, listening to a chorus of frog sounds."}
{"trans": "A brief lifetime of rise, fall, and separation, yet with you I still face the same moon as before."}
{"trans": "The flowers fall, beyond my control; the swallows return, seemingly familiar yet not quite the same."}
{"trans": "At the mountain's foot, short orchid sprouts soak in the stream, the sandy path through pines is clean with no mud, in the whispering evening rain, cuckoos cry."}
{"trans": "Fine rain on the parasol trees, until dusk, falling drop by drop."}
{"trans": "Swallows come flying, asking where spring can be found; only the pond remains green on its own."}
{"trans": "I long to ride the wind and fly back, yet I'm afraid of the jade towers and palaces, where the height is unbearably cold."}
{"trans": "Clearly it was just a beautiful dream, looking back at the east wind, my clothes are filled with tears."}
{"trans": "Over Chu's thousand miles of clear autumn sky, water flows with the horizon into boundless autumn."}
{"trans": "Red beans grow in the southern country, when spring comes, how many branches sprout?"}
{"trans": "The sun rises in the east while it rains in the west; they say there's no sunshine, yet there is sunshine."}
{"trans": "At the place of farewell at Xie Pavilion, the scenery always evokes sorrow."}
{"trans": "His achievements surpassed those in the Three Kingdoms, his fame was established through the Eight Trigrams Formation."}
{"trans": "When flowers bloom and can be picked, one must pick them; don't wait until there are no flowers and only empty branches remain."}
{"trans": "The setting sun is infinitely beautiful, only it's near dusk."}
{"trans": "Charming the night of the third of the ninth moon,\nThe dew like pearls, the moon like a bow."}
{"trans": "After gathering nectar from a hundred flowers to make honey, for whom does one toil and for whom does it taste sweet?"}
{"trans": "A thousand li of yellow clouds, the sun dimmed; North wind blows the wild geese as snow falls thickly."}
{"trans": "Sudden rain from the mountain ahead comes across the stream, washing away all the summer heat of the world."}
{"trans": "Water is a sideways glance, mountains are furrowed brows."}
{"trans": "Scattered rain passes, wind dances wildly through the forest, misty veils and cloud canopies unfold."}
{"trans": "Outside the wall, pedestrians pass; inside, a beauty laughs."}
{"trans": "Hating you is like the moon over the river tower, temporarily full but then waning."}
{"trans": "I will draw the carved bow like a full moon, gazing toward the northwest, to shoot the heavenly wolf."}
{"trans": "The flowing water rushes endlessly without a place to stay, the flying light hurriedly sinks in the west."}
{"trans": "My brain is fried."}
{"trans": "I purple knife clay mend mugwort nest"}
{"trans": "Dying, don't be so hilarious."}
{"trans": "Is this me... going to jail?"}
{"trans": "Laughing so hard I can't stop."}
